'''Blackwing Lair''' is a 40-man raid dungeon located in the [[Blackrock Spire]]<ref name="underdev">[[Underdev/Blackwing Lair]]</ref> section of the [[Blackrock Mountain]] and is the home to [[Nefarian]]. It was implemented in [[patch 1.6]].

==Adventure Guide==
''In the dark recesses of the mountain's peak, Nefarian, the eldest son of Deathwing, conducts some of his most awful experimentation, controlling mighty beings like puppets and combining the eggs of different dragonflights with horrific results.  Should he prove successful, even darker pursuits rest on the horizon.''

''And, yet, the Lord of Blackrock is not a mere scientist - he is a great dragon cornered in his lair.  Can he truly be defeated by mortal hands?''

==History==
Nefarian has vowed to crush [[Ragnaros]]. To this end, he has recently begun efforts to bolster the black dragonflight, much as his father [[Deathwing]] had attempted to do in ages past. However, where Deathwing failed, it now seems the scheming Nefarian may be succeeding. Nefarian's mad bid for dominance has attracted concern from the [[red dragonflight]], which has always been the black flight's greatest foe. Though Nefarian's intentions are known, the methods he is using to achieve them remain a mystery. It is believed, however, that Nefarian has been experimenting with the blood of all of the various [[dragonflight]]s to produce unstoppable warriors, accomplishing what his father failed, the creation of the [[Chromatic dragonflight]].<ref name="underdev" />

Besides the twisted dragonflight, other experiments took place in these halls, including manipulation with dragon bones and eggs. Nefarian also captured and corrupted Vaelastrasz, while his creation [[Chromaggus]] survived and guarded the lair.<ref>''[[World of Warcraft: Exploring Azeroth: The Eastern Kingdoms]]'', pg. 44</ref>

===World of Warcraft===
{{Wow-section}}
[[File:Blackwing Lair Classic key art.jpg|thumb|The [[adventurer]]s facing [[Nefarian]] in his lair.]]
In Year 25 [[ADP]], [[Moira Thaurissan]] sent information on Nefarian and the Dark Horde all over [[Azeroth]], leading the [[Horde]] leadership in [[Orgrimmar]] to learn the truth about their orc brethren in Blackrock Mountain. As such, Horde heroes invaded the lair, cut through the twisted experiments, and slew Nefarian in his sanctuary, taking the [[black dragon]]'s head with them to Orgrimmar.<ref>{{Ref WoWCV3|121}}</ref>

===Cataclysm===
{{Cata-section}}
Following the [[Cataclysm (event)|Cataclysm]] in 28 ADP, Nefarian's broken corpse was collected by the [[Twilight's Hammer]] who brought him back with [[Void]] magic, now an undead monstrosity.<ref>{{Ref WoWCV3|199}}</ref> Dwelling on the lessons learned from his defeat in Blackwing Lair, Nefarian burrowed deeper into the heart of [[Blackrock Mountain]], and rebuilt his sanctuary within the [[Blackwing Descent]].<ref>[http://us.battle.net/wow/en/zone/blackwing-descent/ Blackwing Descent]</ref>

===Exploring Azeroth===
{{Novel-section}}
After the [[Fourth War]] in 34 ADP, [[SI:7]] agents thoroughly investigated the lair and found references to similar experiments that may predate Nefarian. They collected the material for further study.<ref>''[[Exploring Azeroth: The Eastern Kingdoms]]'', pg. 45</ref>

==Geography==
Port in by using the [[Orb of Command]] located at the end of the hall to the right of the entrance to Blackrock Spire (The attunement quest [[Blackhand's Command (quest)]] is no longer necessary and has been removed from the game).

